Code that comes from the three papers integrated by the TCC keeps the copyright of its authors:

  * etapa3_predicao/trajpred/kalman.py and etapa3_predicao/trajpred/sot.py reproduce the external constant-velocity
    Kalman filter and the single-target error protocol of the SIGE 2026 code
    (github.com/IghorRibeiro/hybrid-uav-tracking-prediction, MIT):
    Copyright (c) 2026 Ighor de Souza Ribeiro, Rigel Procópio Fernandes, Gabriel de Sapienza Luna.
  * etapa3_predicao/trajpred/matching.py follows the per-frame evaluation loop of the LAFusion 2026 code
    (github.com/IghorRibeiro/DroneTrackingMOT, AGPL-3.0): same authors.
  * etapa3_predicao/trajpred/hybrid_mot.py extends the hybrid architecture of the SIGE 2026 paper to multiple targets
    and calls, at run time, the Geman-McClure association cost of DroneTrackingMOT.

Ultralytics (AGPL-3.0) - https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
  The detector (YOLO26n) and the trackers are used as a library and are not copied into this repository. The
  Geman-McClure cost and the NSA-Kalman patch, which adapt Ultralytics code, live in DroneTrackingMOT.

OpenCV (Apache-2.0), py-motmetrics (MIT), SciPy, NumPy, pandas and Matplotlib (BSD) are used as libraries.

Datasets (not redistributed): DUT Anti-UAV (Zhao et al., 2022) and Track 3 of the 4th Anti-UAV Challenge
(DOI 10.5281/zenodo.15103888). Each keeps its own license and terms of use.
